{"encoding":"verislop.autonomous-critique/0.1","verdict":"REPAIR","counterexamples":[],"corrections":[{"diagnostic_index":0,"artifact":"formalization.json","explanation":"Retain the capability-gap envelope and every active obligation ID, but expand the attempted alternate representations for UNSUPPORTED_CAPABILITY. Exact nullable integers can be represented by result(error=Unit,ok=Int), preserving null and zero distinctly; this does not supply string comparison or integer-bounded list generation. For a single event {group:'a',time:0,value:1}, start=0,width=1,end=N, O2 requires N output records for arbitrarily large positive N. Finitely nested total folds over the one-element events list and fixed literal lists cannot generate output length depending without bound on N. Likewise, equality, append, length and emptiness do not provide Unicode lexicographic comparison for arbitrary group strings. Retain these precise gaps without replacing the input with presorted groups or caller-provided buckets. The raw Lean alternative must pass the same executable DSL gates, so unrestricted Lean recursion or sorting is not a supported repair. This is an unsupported representation search, not an implementation counterexample or proof of impossibility."}]}